WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.180
- All right, y'all, we have
time for one last story.

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:03.013
I hope you enjoy.

00:00:03.013 --> 00:00:04.299
This as what I'm liking.

00:00:04.299 --> 00:00:08.090
(guitar strumming)
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.090 --> 00:00:09.350
For the past 15 years,

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:12.090
National Geographic
photographer Joel Sartore

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.420
has crisscrossed the globe taking pictures

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.350
of every animal species in human care.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.910
So far he's documented
over 12,000 species.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.000
He calls his project "The Photo Ark,"

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.270
and his goal is to capture these animals

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:26.860
before they disappear.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.150
But he has a bigger goal,

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:30.950
and since it's a new year, we
want to put a spotlight on it.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.300
We have Joel on the line
right now to explain.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.645
What's up, Joel?

00:00:34.645 --> 00:00:36.077
(audience cheering)

00:00:36.077 --> 00:00:36.994
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:39.020
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.800
Your pictures are so
beautiful first of all.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.130
They're so cool.

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:44.940
Is it true that this
project kind of came around

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.481
like unexpectedly so?

00:00:46.481 --> 00:00:47.570
- It did.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:48.410
It did.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:50.390
And believe it or not,
you're part of that story.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:52.069
I bet you didn't even know that.

00:00:52.069 --> 00:00:52.940
- No.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:57.032
- My wife, Kathy, was
diagnosed with breast cancer

00:00:57.032 --> 00:00:58.380
way back when,

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:01.490
when you were just starting
in on American Idol.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:02.323
- [Kelly] Oh wow.

00:01:02.323 --> 00:01:03.900
- And that's been,

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.270
that's what started "The Photo Ark"

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:08.040
was my desire to stay closer to home

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.090
and to do things that didn't take me away

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.460
for months on end.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.700
That's what started "The Photo Ark."

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.350
And you know what we did,

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:18.900
is we watched American Idol
and we watched you win.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:19.733
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:21.023
- And my wife is just fine to this day

00:01:21.023 --> 00:01:22.340
because you cheered her up

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:23.828
and she's sitting right next to me.

00:01:23.828 --> 00:01:25.495
- Oh my gosh, hello.

00:01:27.513 --> 00:01:28.513
I love this.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:34.089
Oh my gosh, oh, I'm gonna cry.

00:01:34.089 --> 00:01:36.540
Well wait, there's a bigger goal

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.293
behind this whole thing though, right?

00:01:38.293 --> 00:01:40.960
- Oh yeah, you bet there
is, you bet there is.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:43.140
We want to teach the
world to love animals,

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:44.810
to introduce them.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.800
And it's like a big
dating service in a way.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.540
Find the animal that you love.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.300
Learn what keeps it thriving
on the face of the earth,

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.990
no matter what walk of life
you come from, no matter what,

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:59.230
let's try to save all these
species in their habitats

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:02.230
because when we save them,
we're actually saving ourselves.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.437
That's the big secret.

00:02:03.437 --> 00:02:04.270
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.550
- We have to have a thriving planet

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:08.570
with all the species that we can imagine

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:10.080
in order to do well ourselves.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.570
We are completely tied to nature.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.620
And so that's what this
project is all about.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:17.010
Get people to learn about animals,

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:18.700
try to figure out what makes them tick,

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.070
what they need in terms
of clean water, clean air,

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:25.830
a healthy forest, healthy
seas, and go forward with them.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.550
Take them forward with us in time

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:30.400
so that we can all enjoy the earth.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:31.370
- Absolutely.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:32.830
And once again,

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.710
the photos are just
breathtakingly beautiful.

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:36.750
I love your work.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:37.780
I'm such a big fan.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.030
Now I'm a fan of you.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:40.080
And that's so awesome

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.560
that y'all watched on Idol 20 years ago.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:42.393
That's so cool.

00:02:42.393 --> 00:02:43.650
That made me feel really good.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:44.880
Thank you for telling me that.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.570
But everybody, if you love these photos,

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:48.087
be sure to get Joel's new book,

00:02:48.087 --> 00:02:49.880
"Photo Ark Wonders:

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.540
Celebrating Diversity
in the Animal Kingdom."

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.390
There's also "Photo Ark ABC."

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.010
This is my favorite for the little ones.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:58.100
My kids are going to freak out over this.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.160
Both books support his ongoing work.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:03.169
Thank you so much, Joel, I'm
liking your post right now.

00:03:03.169 --> 00:03:06.473
And please say hello
again to your wife for me.

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:09.480
But that's not all, Joel.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.560
Usually, this is the point in the show

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:13.420
when our season-long partner Pilot Pen,

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.820
makers of G2, the go-to pin
of the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.841
gives an ultimate overachiever, like Joel,

00:03:17.841 --> 00:03:20.160
a check for $1,000.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.760
But today, Joel's paying it
forward, 'cause he's awesome,

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.570
to give that money to the
National Geographic Society.

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:28.445
Thank you so much, Joel.

00:03:28.445 --> 00:03:30.196
(audience cheering)

00:03:30.196 --> 00:03:31.273
We love you.

00:03:31.273 --> 00:03:32.106
- Thank you.

00:03:32.106 --> 00:03:34.453
- [Kelly] And we appreciate
you and we love this art.

